<title>USA: Court okays Los Angeles tobacco industry suit.</title>
<headline>Court okays Los Angeles tobacco industry suit.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A judge Friday gave the green light for Los Angeles county to go ahead with its suit against the &quot;Big Six&quot; tobacco companies for hundreds of millions of dollars in health costs related to treating smoking-related illnesses.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Los Angeles County Board of Supervisors Chairman Zev Yaroslavsky said San Diego Superior Court Judge Robert May refused the tobacco industry's effort to dismiss the lawsuit.</p>
</text>
